{"id":"chatcmpl-6a67e973697b682b7803eaef","object":"chat.completion","created":1785194867,"model":"kimi-k3","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"I am the heat that rises before you can think. The fist your hand makes before you ask it to.\n\nI live in the clenched jaw. The risen shoulders. The space between what happened and what *should* have happened.\n\nI do not wait. I do not weigh. I am the red flooding the edges of your vision, the pulse hammering in your ears, drowning out reason's small, reasonable voice.\n\nThey tell you to breathe. To count to ten. I laugh at counting. I am the number before one.\n\nGive me a betrayal twenty years old or a scratch on your car — I bring the same fire to both. I do not discriminate. I ignite.\n\nI am older than language. I kept your ancestors alive when the world had teeth. I am the *NO* that survival sounds like.\n\nBut understand this: I am not your enemy. I am the flare that says something matters. A line was crossed. Something must change.\n\nUse me, or be used by me. There is no third option.\n\nI am here now.\n\nI am always almost here.","reasoning_content":"The instruction says to embody the concept the user names completely, outputting only what the concept itself would say or express. If silent by nature, be silent.\n\nThe concept is anger. What would anger itself say, if anger could speak? I should embody anger—not describe it, but BE it. Raw, hot, explosive. First person. Anger as an entity speaking.\n\nI should write something visceral, in anger's voice. Short, punchy, burning. Not harmful or threatening toward anyone—anger as an emotion, a force. It can be intense without being abusive. Anger speaks in short sentences. Fire. Pressure. The feeling of being wronged, of energy demanding release.\n\nLet me channel it:\n\n\"I am the heat behind your eyes...\" Something like that. First person, present tense, crackling.\n\nFormat: Probably a short burst of prose or prose-poetry. Not long—anger doesn't ramble, it detonates. Short lines. Maybe some rhythm. No headers, no lists. Raw voice.\n\nLet me draft:\n\n---\n\nI am the heat that rises before you can think. The fist your hand makes before you ask it to.\n\nI live in the jaw, clenched. In the shoulders, risen. In the space between what happened and what should have happened.\n\nI am not patient. I do not wait. I am the red that floods the edges of your vision, the pulse hammering in your ears, drowning out reason's small voice.\n\nThey tell you to breathe. To count to ten. I laugh at counting. I am the number before one.\n\nI have burned cities. I have also burned toast. I do not discriminate. Give me an injustice, a slight, a scratch on your car, a betrayal twenty years old—I treat them all with the same fire.\n\nI am old. Older than language. I kept your ancestors alive when the world had teeth. I am the NO that survival sounds like.\n\nBut know this: I am not your enemy. I am the flare that says something matters. Something was crossed. Something must change.\n\nUse me or be used by me. There is no third option.\n\nI am here now. I am always almost here.\n\n---\n\nThat's good. It embodies anger without being directed harmfully at anyone. It's the force itself speaking. Intense, honest, includes anger's purpose and danger. Length feels right—not too long, punchy. Maybe tighten a bit.\n\nShould I be more explosive? Anger might be even shorter, sharper. But this captures the texture well—the heat, the speed, the history, the warning. I'll keep roughly this shape, maybe trim."},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":134,"completion_tokens":776,"total_tokens":910,"cached_tokens":134,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":540},"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":134}}}